  body: "# Living together as a married couple in DMG chapter 11\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter describes
    considering the whole relationship and the totality of evidence, with no single factor deciding whether people
    are living together as a married couple.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nScope depends on the benefit and preliminary
    conditions in DMG 11005–11006. The chapter explicitly sends Universal Credit to ADM E4. Historic dated pages
    and cited cases need current-law review; no inference about a real person’s relationship is authorised.\n\n\
    ## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 11021, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a820c1ae5274a2e8ab5738a/dmgch11.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 11: Living together as husband and wife or as civil partners .\n- [DMG 11101, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a820c1ae5274a2e8ab5738a/dmgch11.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 11: Living together as husband and wife or as civil partners .\n- [DMG 11103, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a820c1ae5274a2e8ab5738a/dmgch11.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 11: Living together as husband and wife or as civil partners .\n- [DMG 11107, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a820c1ae5274a2e8ab5738a/dmgch11.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 11: Living together as husband and wife or as civil partners .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\
    \nModel-assisted interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist
    review. The source is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental
    publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page
    numbers are one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters.
    Quoted relationships preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal
    effects and current applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch11` PDF SHA-256: `1f83a691baec9f1ff9f946289647f53b1b4b3b91788c4f39f71983b136382289`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `73fbd1921b0dcf803d66aab7915a768921372438265b337362b080284bc6e59f`.\n"
